                <invention-title lang="en">METHOD OF ROTOR PRODUCTION INCLUDING CO-CURING AND MAGNETIZATION IN PLACE</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Techniques described here provide a rotor and a method of making a rotor. In an embodiment, a method of making a rotor includes forming a magnet array by assembling a plurality of magnets into the magnet array, providing pre-preg adjacent to the magnet array, co-curing the magnet array with the pre-preg, and magnetizing the magnet array subsequent to the formation of the magnet array.</p>
